@startuml
title UC-03 - Checkout COD with idempotency
skinparam shadowing false
actor Customer
participant "Checkout UI" as UI
participant "Cart / PurchaseApi" as APP
participant "Supabase RPC\ncreate_food_order" as RPC
database PostgreSQL as DB
Customer -> UI : Confirm address, recipient, vouchers
UI -> APP : Validate and reuse/create request UUID
APP -> RPC : JWT + UUID + items + location + recipient
RPC -> RPC : Check session and request owner
RPC -> DB : Acquire transaction lock / find request
alt Same request already completed
  DB --> RPC : Existing order
  RPC --> APP : Existing order
else New request
  RPC -> DB : Read catalog, options, vouchers
  RPC -> RPC : Recalculate prices, shipping, range
  alt Invalid input or changed price
    RPC --> APP : Business error
    APP --> UI : Keep cart, show correction
  else Valid
    RPC -> DB : Insert order, items, snapshots\nand related voucher changes in transaction
    alt Any database operation fails
      DB --> RPC : Rollback
      RPC --> APP : Error
      APP --> UI : Keep cart / same retry UUID
    else Commit succeeds
      DB --> RPC : Order
      RPC --> APP : Confirmed order
    end
  end
end
opt Confirmed successful result received
  APP -> APP : Clear cart after confirmation
  APP --> UI : Navigate to tracking(orderId)
  UI --> Customer : Show server invoice
end
note over APP,RPC
If the response is lost, retry the same request UUID.
Do not assume failure means no order was created.
end note
@enduml
